{
 "title": "Métodos e impl",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Para añadir comportamiento a un tipo escribes un bloque **`impl`**. El primer parámetro de un método es `self`; accedes a los campos del objeto con `self.campo`. Una llamada se ve así: `objeto.metodo()`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "struct Rectangle:",
    "    width: f64",
    "    height: f64",
    "",
    "impl Rectangle:",
    "    fn area(self) -> f64:",
    "        return self.width * self.height",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    rect = Rectangle{ width: 10.0, height: 5.0 }",
    "    print(\"Area:\", rect.area())"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Area: 50"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Un método que cambia el objeto en el sitio escribe `self: lend Tipo` (aprenderás `lend` en el capítulo 5: \"tomar prestado y cambiar\"). Los métodos que no reciben `self` son métodos **estáticos** y se usan a menudo como constructores: `Tipo.nombre(...)`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "struct Player:",
    "    name: str",
    "    health: i32",
    "",
    "impl Player:",
    "    fn new(name: str) -> Player:",
    "        return Player{ name: name, health: 100 }",
    "",
    "    fn is_alive(self) -> bool:",
    "        return self.health > 0",
    "",
    "    fn take_damage(self: lend Player, amount: i32):",
    "        self.health -= amount",
    "        if self.health < 0:",
    "            self.health = 0",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    hero = Player.new(\"Aragorn\")",
    "    hero.take_damage(35)",
    "    print(\"Health:\", hero.health)",
    "    print(\"Alive?\", hero.is_alive())"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Health: 65",
    "Alive? true"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c04-l02-x1",
   "prompt": "Añade un método `increment` al struct `Counter` (`value: i32`): aumenta `value` en 1. Llámalo tres veces e imprime `value`.",
   "starter": [
    "struct Counter:",
    "    value: i32",
    "",
    "impl Counter:",
    "    fn increment(self: lend Counter):",
    "        pass",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    c = Counter{ value: 0 }",
    "    c.increment()",
    "    c.increment()",
    "    c.increment()",
    "    print(c.value)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "struct Counter:",
    "    value: i32",
    "",
    "impl Counter:",
    "    fn increment(self: lend Counter):",
    "        self.value += 1",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    c = Counter{ value: 0 }",
    "    c.increment()",
    "    c.increment()",
    "    c.increment()",
    "    print(c.value)"
   ],
   "hint": "Sustituye `pass` por `self.value += 1`.",
   "expected": [
    "3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c04-l02-q1",
   "q": "¿Cómo se llama un método sin `self`?",
   "options": [
    "Método privado",
    "Método estático (a menudo un constructor)",
    "Método roto"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "Los métodos que se llaman como `Player.new(...)` son estáticos."
  }
 ]
